\taxon{Discussion}
\title{Mass, transport and the connection weight}
\date{2026-11-09}

\p{A [charged lattice field](fdip-009O) compares neighboring spinors by parallel transport. Its [paired coefficient integral](fdip-008H) gives a determinant. The [Wilson term](fdip-009U) adds a nonnegative second difference to the skew Dirac operator. Which mass and spin symmetries make the resulting determinant a positive weight on every connection?}
